<article class="env-remark" id="6C51A4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/6C51A4">Remark <span data-tag="6C51A4">7.2.1.5</span>.</a> If $\calX $ is a coproduct (in the $\infty $-category $\RGeom $) of $\infty $-topoi $\calX _{\alpha }$, then $\calX $ is of homotopy dimension $\leq n$ if and only if each $\calX _{\alpha }$ is of homotopy dimension $\leq n$. </p>
